From 05d963d4be1e7d4ca9f72f73b783e8970e9d8767 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:11:53 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix: point app at new rental_vehicles/rental_bookings tables
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The homepage's "Couldn't load live vehicles: Could not find a
relationship between 'vehicles' and 'suppliers' in the schema cache"
error was a database-side issue, not a code bug: this Supabase project
already had tables named vehicles/bookings, but they belonged to an
unrelated car-wash-shaped schema (customer_id, vehicle_type, service_id,
booking_date/time) with no supplier_id relationship at all. The rental
marketplace's own vehicles/bookings tables were never actually created.

Added rental_vehicles and rental_bookings tables (with the FKs,
check/exclusion constraints, RLS policies, triggers, and the
previously-missing get_supplier_document_url RPC that the rest of the
schema — suppliers/invoices/disputes/reviews/profiles — already
expected), leaving the car-wash tables untouched. This commit repoints
every sbSelect/sbInsert/sbUpdate/useRealtimeRefresh call and embedded
select (vehicles:rental_vehicles(...), bookings:rental_bookings(...))
at the new tables.

